{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413504-how-extensive-is-a-god-s-ability-how-much-can-they-change-what-can-truly-kill-them","id":1413504,"title":"How extensive is a god's ability? How much can they change? What can truly kill them?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-14T00:59:26-07:00","id":1413504,"title":"How extensive is a god's ability? How much can they change? What can truly kill them?","content":"Let's say there was a god of a place - a city that has been destroyed but still exists in ruins. This god has become itinerate but is still connected to its point of origin. What methods would dragonbloods have available to them to find out the specific nature of this god? I know there are occult charms for solars but even those I've never figured out how you just find out the origin of something that no one actually knows but them. Other than compelling or forcing it? Is there any way to access information &quot;contained in essence&quot; without actually having a person (the god themselves or someone who knew them) confirm it? Is there a roster in heaven for all creation's gods, no matter how obscure?<br /> <br /> And finally - how much can a god's nature really change? Assuming this was a first age city which is &quot;dead&quot; and &quot;ruined&quot; but not &quot;gone&quot; - the god still exists, I'm guessing. The city's name has lived on in legend, and inspired treasure seekers - even if none have found it the name of it is still alive and well on the lips of travelers everywhere in this direction of the celestial compass. The god is still &quot;alive&quot; because the name and legends of the city are, but the NATURE of it has diminished so that I'm curious if that god, with travel and learning, could accumulate other qualities? I know gods aren't like mortals, but are they capable of change? Maybe even growth? What can change the nature of a god? (Planescape voice)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4407-loving-the-gorgon","name":"Loving the Gorgon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4407_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T02:44:15-07:00","id":1413516,"title":"","content":"For your first part, I guess if the city is in ruined, it would be cool to have to find a fallen temple with registers of this god's domain or something like that. Solars have a cheat code to look at things and bypass scenario, but you can still decide to do a normal scenario for anything else (like DBs) where they have to find the information by looking for it. Maybe there are complex runes in a ruined temple that can allow to understand the nature of the god thanks fo Occult rolls and combine it with a Linguistics roll and Investigation roll to find and decipher the ancient texts that were hidden the temple. <br /> <br /> For the second part, naturally I don't know the extend to which a god can change, but a god in a First Age ruin that has seen millennia passing by can most surely change. I tend to like to add some kind of &quot;magical dementias&quot; for powerful beings that are isolated for long, to illustrate the hardship of loneliness for so long. Maybe he has reconstructed some kind of phantasmic illusions that relive the glorious days, or he has fallen a bit to darkness and went into dark arts to try to revive worshippers, resulting in something that is half a god and half a very small Neverborn. I tend to play the &quot;WoW corruption card&quot; a lot if there is the possibility of a Wyld Zone or a Shadowlands, to make half-normal half-changed things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T03:07:59-07:00","id":1413518,"title":"","content":"There may well be a register of divinities in Heaven, but good luck getting Jupiter to share.<br /> <br /> Ahlat started out as the Bull God, and now he's the Southern War God. So yes, spirits can change and grow over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T04:40:20-07:00","id":1413524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrFamiliar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413504-how-extensive-is-a-god-s-ability-how-much-can-they-change-what-can-truly-kill-them?p=1413518#post1413518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahlat started out as the Bull God, and now he's the Southern War God. So yes, spirits can change and grow over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahlat started out of a Northern God of Walrus Mating Rituals, who was promoted to Southern God of Cattle for leading bull walruses against a fair folk incursion, and then finessed his way into adding &quot;and War&quot; to his portfolio by encouraging cattle raids between the tribes.<br /> <br /> So... yeah... change is a thing that happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 09-14-2020, 07:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T04:45:12-07:00","id":1413527,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loving the Gorgon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413504-how-extensive-is-a-god-s-ability-how-much-can-they-change-what-can-truly-kill-them#post1413504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say there was a god of a place - a city that has been destroyed but still exists in ruins. This god has become itinerate but is still connected to its point of origin. What methods would dragonbloods have available to them to find out the specific nature of this god? I know there are occult charms for solars but even those I've never figured out how you just find out the origin of something that no one actually knows but them. Other than compelling or forcing it? Is there any way to access information &quot;contained in essence&quot; without actually having a person (the god themselves or someone who knew them) confirm it?</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I feel it's perfectly in keeping with the Occult Ability, particularly assisted by Charms, to acquire a bit of information in a divinatory manner, although I'd be personally inclined to include elements of observation and deduction with references. If an person can tell that this is a detached city god, then they might identify signifiers in appearance and mannerisms that suggest what city the god came from, or even be recognised in records describing the god back in better days. Depending on the character looking for that information, that could alternately take the form of &quot;note the features to check against next time I have access to some books&quot; or already being scholarly enough to recall or follow lines of reasoning to make accurate conclusions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loving the Gorgon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Is there a roster in heaven for all creation's gods, no matter how obscure?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It would seem to be in keeping with depictions of Yu-Shan that they keep records identifying almost all gods, but I think it's also in keeping that such records are widely distributed and not conveniently organised; there's not a convenient and centralised card catalogue or other database to know where to find any specific piece of information you're looking for.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In keeping, and also my own preference to prevent Yu-Shan from being an immediate source of all desirable knowledge.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loving the Gorgon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And finally - how much can a god's nature really change? Assuming this was a first age city which is &quot;dead&quot; and &quot;ruined&quot; but not &quot;gone&quot; - the god still exists, I'm guessing. The city's name has lived on in legend, and inspired treasure seekers - even if none have found it the name of it is still alive and well on the lips of travelers everywhere in this direction of the celestial compass. The god is still &quot;alive&quot; because the name and legends of the city are</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The continued existence of gods is not so deeply tied to their domains, nor is their power exactly dependent on mortal regard or awareness; a city can have nothing so much as foundations left and nobody remembering it, and its patron deity would not simply fade from existence. I think that for the most part a god would want to preserve some of the reputation of such a lost city for the satisfaction of their ego or sense of self; not a metaphysical thing as such, more like a has-been actor who'll often try to remind people of their bigger parts back in the day.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">There's some loss of power (in this particular case I think largely from a lack of the appropriate targets to work Charms upon), but not necessarily being reduced to a wisp. I can also imagine the god might want to leverage their history, reputation and capabilities into being adopted as the spirit of a new city, if somebody wished to establish one.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I expect that the biggest concern for this kind of god in particular is the loss of a sanctum, which apart from being a pleasant place to live allows the god to recover from being slain by something less than Exalted spirit-killing Charms.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loving the Gorgon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">the NATURE of it has diminished so that I'm curious if that god, with travel and learning, could accumulate other qualities? I know gods aren't like mortals, but are they capable of change? Maybe even growth? What can change the nature of a god?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For the first one, sure, gods can change in the sense of differences in outlook depending on who they know and what they know, which might affect how they choose to go about things in their lives. I do think it would be fitting for the god of a totally ruined city to take in a bit of that quality of desolation and emptiness, although maybe more as a bit of colour for their existing Charms rather than totally new ones. I think it's appropriate for such a god to change again if they become attached to a new city, to adhere with some of its character or values or needs.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The big things that might cause alterations to a god are reassignment or promotion within the Celestial Hierarchy. And previous Editions have given Sidereals some magic to bring about changes in keeping with giving gods new areas of responsibility.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Actually... Fangs at the Gate has some examples of gods that rebranded, let me just check... yeah, you've got things like the god of wells for a Southern city-state taking up the function of finding and blessing oases and a granary guardian becoming a protector of the health of herds when the people are forced to become pastoral nomads. I infer a capacity to reapply themselves, but a preference to stay with what is familiar.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrFamiliar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413504-how-extensive-is-a-god-s-ability-how-much-can-they-change-what-can-truly-kill-them?p=1413518#post1413518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahlat started out as the Bull God, and now he's the Southern War God. So yes, spirits can change and grow over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>He actually started out as god over walrus mating competitions. He got himself promoted to Southern Cattle God, and then when his actions helped produce a good pool of candidates for warrior Exalted, rose to Southern God of War and Cattle (these things still being intertwined in his milieu).<br /> <br /> There's an observable through line between a god starting out as guardian of an animal's violent courtship practices and becoming a war god with distinct animal motifs, and even then his rise was facilitated by procedure and patronage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}